not everyone is able to spend their  Christmas with loved ones  if it wasn't for pubs cafes and  Community groups opening their doors  thousands would spend it alone I would  be back in Canary Wharf right now and  I'd probably be alone in my little flat  it's just I don't know it's such a gift  it really is like in this moment I  wasn't sure I felt brave enough and I  was thinking of all reasons not to call  but the Highlight is being so welcome I  think it's just such a fantastic  opportunity for so many different people  to come together and people that I  wouldn't ordinarily have interacted with  or met otherwise the number of people  relying on the generosity of others is  on the rise this Pub in Wimbledon was  packed offering free food friendship and  warmth for those in need I just think  it's one of those things that you know  if you sit in the house on your own  you're going to get a lot of people do  we've got nowhere to go for it for a lot  of different reasons and it's much  better for our mental health and all the  rest if we come out and we mix other  people and have a bit of a laugh and  what we're trying to do really is break  down that kind of uh stigma where if  you're on you're not gonna be ashamed of  anyone can end up lonely over Christmas  for a whole host of reasons but  admitting isolation can be pretty scary  and with the cost of living crisis  taking its grip across the country many  won't just be lonely this Christmas  they'll be cold and hungry too is it  morning yeah this community group in  Birmingham is one of many set up across  the country offering a safe place on  Christmas Day and they say this year has  been busier than ever we've had to work  with other Charities to signpost people  elsewhere because we haven't been able  to meet the demands so the demand is  outstriping the event the ability that  we've got to provide on such large  numbers so we've worked with partner  organizations so that we can make sure  people get the help and support that  they need and after a difficult year  dominated by news of financial pressure  it seems that more people than usual  relied on the kindness of strangers to  help see them through which is what  Christmas is all about  Shimon Freeman Powell Sky News
 

